Rules:
  [K1] Use topics for event streams.
  [K2] Use partitions for parallelism.
  [K3] Use consumer groups for scaling.
  [K4] Use keys for ordering within partition.
  [K5] Use schema registry for contracts.
  [K6] Use exactly-once semantics when needed.
  [K7] Monitor with Kafka Manager.
  [K8] Size partitions for throughput.

Pros:
  - High throughput
  - Distributed
  - Persistent logs

Cons:
  - Operational complexity
  - Resource intensive
  - Learning curve

Alternatives:
  - NATS (simpler)
  - RabbitMQ (traditional)
  - Pulsar (modern)

State: +

